course: dictionary
lesson: 4681
title: One word, many meanings: home
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: The word home has more than one meaning. Context clues tell you which meaning is right. In «Ruby ran home after school», home tells you where she went: to the place where she lives.
explain: Home can also be a noun, as in «The family was happy in their new home», where it means the house they live in. It can be an adjective too, as in «our home address», where home tells you which address.
explain: Look at the words around it. In «The elder brother, who had stayed at home, was angry», the clue is stayed: he stayed in the place where he lives. Swap in another word, such as house, and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Home can be a noun, an adverb or an adjective.
fact: «Home» means the place where you live, with your family.
fact: «Home» can also mean the base you try to reach in a game, and the home team plays on its own ground.
fact: An animal's home is where it lives, like a nest or burrow.
fact: Formal words such as residence and dwelling mean the same as home in official writing.
exercise: «Ruby ran home after school.» What does home mean here? | A house for sale | *To the place where she lives | To a game base | A nest in a tree
exercise: «The home team won the match in front of their fans.» What does home team mean? | A team from another country | A team with no players | A team that lives in a house | *The team playing on its own ground
exercise: «The fox's home is a den under the roots.» What is a fox's home? | *The place where it lives | A bell it wears on its collar | A school for foxes | Its favourite food
test: «Mum said the elder brother had stayed at home.» What does at home mean here? | Out in the rain | At school | *In the place where he lives with his family | In a football game
test: In «The family bought a new home», which word could you swap in to keep the same meaning? | nest | game | team | *house
exam: In a formal letter, which word could replace home in «the address of our home»? | *residence | team | run | nest
